<text top="139" left="129" width="52" height="10" font="2"><b>Student:</b></text>
<text top="139" left="185" width="274" height="14" font="3"><i>(sighing) Professors have all the control, it seems...</i></text>
<text top="159" left="129" width="61" height="10" font="2"><b>Professor:</b></text>
<text top="159" left="196" width="365" height="14" font="3"><i>Oh, hardly! But that little control they do get to exercise is one of</i></text>
<text top="174" left="129" width="432" height="14" font="3"><i>the fun parts of the job. Deciding on assignments is important you know — and</i></text>
<text top="189" left="129" width="225" height="14" font="3"><i>not something any professor takes lightly.</i></text>
<text top="209" left="129" width="52" height="10" font="2"><b>Student:</b></text>
<text top="209" left="187" width="374" height="14" font="3"><i>Well, that is good to hear. I guess we should see what these projects</i></text>
<text top="224" left="129" width="77" height="14" font="3"><i>are all about...</i></text>
<text top="245" left="129" width="61" height="10" font="2"><b>Professor:</b></text>
<text top="244" left="197" width="364" height="14" font="3"><i>OK. And one more thing: if you’re interested in the systems pro-</i></text>
<text top="259" left="129" width="284" height="14" font="3"><i>gramming part, there is also a little tutorial about the</i></text>
<text top="259" left="416" width="10" height="12" font="5">U</text>
<text top="261" left="427" width="21" height="10" font="6">NIX</text>
<text top="259" left="451" width="109" height="14" font="3"><i>and C programming</i></text>
<text top="274" left="129" width="73" height="14" font="3"><i>environment.</i></text>
<text top="295" left="129" width="52" height="10" font="2"><b>Student:</b></text>
<text top="295" left="185" width="193" height="14" font="3"><i>Sounds almost too useful to be true.</i></text>
<text top="315" left="129" width="61" height="10" font="2"><b>Professor:</b></text>
<text top="315" left="195" width="366" height="14" font="3"><i>Well, take a look. You know, classes are supposed to be about useful</i></text>
<text top="330" left="129" width="102" height="14" font="3"><i>things, sometimes!</i></text>
